{"chapter": 1, "sha256": "5f7bf519a2b686c5d34bd89bb18bed0125ad0a2bd7860427188e86c179e9221a", "voice": {"voice_id": "ppLqTilh7rH7fbUVlXsf", "name": "David - Documentary", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "voice_settings": {"stability": 0.5, "similarity_boost": 0.8, "style": 0.0, "use_speaker_boost": true}}, "source": "docs/script.md", "files": {"narration": {"file": "ch1.mp3", "text": "The Sphinx was not built. It was carved from bedrock, so the walls of its ditch are as old as the statue.\n\nThe geologist Robert Schoch read those walls as rain-cut: soft beds cut back into coves, fissures widest at the top. Wind and sand, he says, cut sharp level grooves. Even Colin Reader, who rejects his date, agrees water cut them. Archaeologists answer that the ditch was Khafre's quarry.\n\nThen he looked under the floor. A 1992 seismic survey, by his account, found the rock weathered about two metres deep in front and a little over one behind. Deeper means longer exposed, so the front was cut first. On his most cautious reckoning the core is at least seven thousand years old; he prefers about 10,000 BCE. Other geologists say the rock's own layers could explain the difference.", "seconds": 58.0, "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", " ", "S", "p", "h", "i", "n", "x", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "n", "o", "t", " ", "b", "u", "i", "l", "t", ".", " ", "I", "t", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "c", "a", "r", "v", "e", "d", " ", "f", "r", "o", "m", " ", "b", "e", "d", "r", "o", "c", "k", ",", " ", "s", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "w", "a", "l", "l", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "i", "t", "s", " ", "d", "i", "t", "c", "h", " ", "a", "r", "e", " ", "a", "s", " ", "o", "l", "d", " ", "a", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "t", "a", "t", "u", "e", ".", "\n", "\n", "T", "h", "e", " ", "g", "e", "o", "l", "o", "g", "i", "s", "t", " ", "R", "o", "b", "e", "r", "t", " ", "S", "c", "h", "o", "c", "h", " ", "r", "e", "a", "d", " ", "t", "h", "o", "s", "e", " ", "w", "a", "l", "l", "s", " ", "a", "s", " ", "